(docs/'ITERATION.md').write_text('# Why five probes became two\n\n'+'\n\n'.join('## '+t+'\n\n'+s for _,t,s in TIMELINE)+'\n\n## Selection criterion\n\nReduce barriers of knowledge, language, manual skill, arriving alone and willingness to use AI. Prototype feedback helps identify useful participation improvements.\n\nKeep 1 as an introduction. Develop 2 as A. Pause 3. Merge 4 and 5 as B.\n\n[Full five-probe table](COMPARISON.md) · [A](PROBE_A.md) · [B](PROBE_B.md)\n',encoding='utf-8')
(docs/'COMPARISON.md').write_text('# Five-probe evaluation and initial selection\n\nOne continuous table links the initial ideas, current activities, questions, theory, speculation, feedback and decision. The Round 1 low-fidelity test is defined by ERGO 117392 V1.0 dated 22 October 2026.\n\n| '+' | '.join(HEADERS)+' |\n| '+' | '.join('---' for _ in HEADERS)+' |\n'+''.join('| '+' | '.join(strip(c).replace('|',' / ') for c in row)+' |\n' for row in ROWS)+'\n\n[Original speculation passages](SPECULATION.md) · [Numeric references](SOURCES.md)\n',encoding='utf-8')
for d in DIRECTIONS:
    md=f'# Direction {d["letter"]} · {d["title"]}\n\n{d["origin"]}. Working concept under iterative development. See [Round 1](FIRST_STAGE_TEST.md) for the first low-fidelity implementation.\n\n{d["sentence"]}\n\n## Research question\n\n{d["rq"]}\n\n{d["purpose"]}\n\n## Intended probe interaction\n\n'
    md+='\n\n'.join(f'{i}. **{t}.** {s}' for i,(t,s) in enumerate(d['steps'],1))
